   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A tank holds \\( V(t) \\) liters of water shared equally among \\( N(t) \\) animals, where \\( t \\) is measured in days. At \\( t = 3 \\), \\( V(3) = 50 \\), \\( V'(3) = -3 \\), \\( N(3) = 3 \\), and \\( N'(3) = 2 \\). The water per animal is \\( W(t) = \\frac{V(t)}{N(t)} \\) liters. Find the value of \\( W'(3) \\), in liters per animal per day."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         -109,
         9
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Record the values at \\( t = 3 \\): \\( V(3) = 50 \\), \\( V'(3) = -3 \\), \\( N(3) = 3 \\), \\( N'(3) = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": -3
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the quotient rule, \\( \\left(\\frac{V}{N}\\right)'(3) = \\frac{V'(3)N(3) - V(3)N'(3)}{[N(3)]^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": 50
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute: \\( \\frac{(-3)(3) - (50)(2)}{(3)^{2}} = \\frac{-109}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -109,
            9
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( W'(3) = - \\frac{109}{9} \\) liters per animal per day at \\( t = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -109,
            9
         ]
      }
   ],
